Optimize this fixed combinational instance: module alu_64bit, parameters {}. Minimize mapped maximum data arrival. Give one complete synthesizable Verilog-2001 design. Keep module, parameters, ports, widths, signedness, truncations, priority and default-case behavior. All inputs are unconstrained, all outputs must match for every two-state input. No clocks, storage, latency, assumptions, external includes, or new dependencies. Helper modules are allowed.
Common evaluation: SKY130HD TT25C1.80V; zero external IO delays; input transition0.10ns; output load0.010pF; 100ns virtual reporting clock; no physical wire parasitics. Yosys flatten/synth-noabc; ABC strash/dretime/map/cleanup-i-o/buffer/upsize/dnsize/stime-p with fixed driver and load. Full source and mapped equivalence and zero electrical violations required.
Baseline mapped area 11907.670400um^2; fixed cap 13098.437440um^2. No candidate results are supplied.
Return exactly one JSON object with these six fields: candidate_rtl, bottleneck, rewrite, expected_timing_gain, area_or_other_cost, functional_boundaries.
Original RTL:
module alu_64bit(
    input [63:0] a, b,
    input [2:0] Oper,
    output reg [63:0] sum
);
reg c_out;
always @(*) begin
    case(Oper)
        3'b000:  {c_out,sum} = a + b;
        3'b001:  {c_out,sum} = a - b;
        3'b010:  {c_out,sum} = b - a;
        3'b011:  {c_out,sum} = a | b;
        3'b100:  {c_out,sum} = a & b;
        3'b101:  {c_out,sum} = a ^ b;
        3'b110:  {c_out,sum} = a ~^ b;
        default: {c_out,sum} = 65'b0;
    endcase
end
endmodule
